=====Chamber 1=====
======The Craftsman======
Speak to the elderly man in the first chamber, and he asks if you are planning to explore the cave. He makes a request: bring him some [[Shoal Salt]]s and [[Shoal Shell]]s, and he will craft something useful for you. Shoal Shells are found at high tide, while Shoal Salts are found at low tide. These resources are replenished each day, so there's no limit to the number collected. Bring him four of each item, and he fashions them into a [[Shell Bell]].

Move northward and take the north-central doorway to the next chamber.

=====Chamber 2=====
Climb up the stairway and continue north. Turn eastward and climb down the east-central ladder.

=====Chamber 3=====
Pick up the [[Shoal Salt]] and [[Ice Heal]], then climb northward and take the northwest ladder.

=====Chamber 2=====
Move west over the larger bridge, then east over the smaller one. Climb down the ladder in the center of the chamber.

=====Chamber 4=====
Go east to find a Black Belt; speak to him to receive a [[Focus Band]]. Continue east to find another [[Shoal Salt]]. Use {{m|Strength}} to move the boulder eastward, then climb down the southeast ladder.

=====Chamber 5=====
The deepest chamber is permanently encased in ice, and the slippery floors make travel difficult. Slide southward across the first two ice patches. At the third patch, slide westward to the small clear spot in the center, then north to a larger clear spot. Take one step westward, then slide south and west to the final small clear spot; move south, east, then north from here to continue on. At the final ice patch, slide north to the small clear spot; move west, south, east, then north from here to reach the elevated ridge. Collect the [[Never-Melt Ice|NeverMeltIce]] from its south end. Return to the clear spot near the stairway, then slide to the cavern's northwest corner. Move east, then south to a larger clear spot. Slide north to the rock near the northwest corner. Move east, south, and west to the rock next to the ridge. Slide north, west, south, then west again to reach the small clear spot. Finally, move north, east, then south to reach {{TM|07|Hail}}.
